# charlie-work fleet scheduler — crontab entry for periodic invocation.
# Add this line to your crontab (crontab -e) to run charlie fleet bash-rats
# at the specified interval. Detection latency equals invocation cadence:
# a stalled session found on pass N is invisible until pass N+1 runs.
# There is no daemon — this design does not add one. Choose your interval
# based on how quickly you need to detect stalled/runaway/dead workers.
#
# Example: Run every 5 minutes (adjust the interval as needed)
# */5 * * * * cd /path/to/your/repo && charlie fleet bash-rats >> /var/log/charlie-work.log 2>&1
#
# For single-repo (non-fleet) usage, replace `charlie fleet bash-rats` with
# `charlie bash-rats` and adjust the repo path accordingly.
